      "role": "user",
      "content": "it just feels so irrational, you know? like, we spend our whole lives building these tiny, temporary structures of meaning—relationships, careers, even just memories—knowing they're all going to be erased. if the universe is just vast, indifferent nothingness, then all this effort to keep ourselves going is basically just a glitch in the system. it feels like we're just prolonging the inevitable for no actual reason.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
